WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.329
Everyone in the school auditorium was quiet.

2
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.475
We were waiting for Mr. Bright to call out the name of the winner.

3
00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:17.689
"And the winner is Evan Demarco for his Automatic Fish-Feeder!" cried Mr. Bright.

4
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.778
Evan stood up, and everyone clapped and cheered.

5
00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.167
I clapped too, but I was stunned.

6
00:00:25.168 --> 00:00:28.898
I felt like a balloon with all the air let out.

7
00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:32.286
I was Iggy the Incredible Inventor.

8
00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:34.144
But I had not won!

9
00:00:34.145 --> 00:00:38.955
Neither of my inventions would be in The Kids' Invention Guide

10
00:00:38.956 --> 00:00:43.697
. I could understand Mr. Bright not choosing the Fabulous

11
00:00:43.698 --> 00:00:46.441
Glasses-Finder. But what about my

12
00:00:46.442 --> 00:00:54.719
Pick-a-Number? All the kids had loved that

13
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.740
invention! On the way out of the assembly, Evan came up to

14
00:00:59.741 --> 00:01:02.718
me. "Thanks, Iggy!" he

15
00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:05.603
said. "For what?" I

16
00:01:05.604 --> 00:01:09.735
asked. "For inspiring me to invent something," said

17
00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.931
Evan. I looked at

18
00:01:11.932 --> 00:01:13.890
him. "What do you

19
00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:18.073
mean?" "You always invent such cool things," he

20
00:01:18.074 --> 00:01:21.182
said. "So I wanted to invent something cool

21
00:01:21.183 --> 00:01:24.231
too." "Oh," I answered with a

22
00:01:24.232 --> 00:01:27.189
smile. "Well, congratulations for

23
00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:31.478
winning. Your Automatic Fish-Feeder is a great

24
00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:34.958
idea." I felt better, knowing I had inspired

25
00:01:34.959 --> 00:01:39.296
Evan. But I still couldn't help feeling a little

26
00:01:39.297 --> 00:01:44.202
disappointed. After school Jenny, Josh, Molly, and I went to the

27
00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:50.981
park. "My teacher said I can take my math and spelling tests again," Jenny told us

28
00:01:50.982 --> 00:01:55.849
happily. "And I can see all the way across the park

29
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.940
now." A second later Jenny

30
00:01:58.941 --> 00:02:02.377
gasped. "Look! It's Mr.

31
00:02:02.378 --> 00:02:08.016
Bright!" Sure enough, there was Mr. Bright on the other side of the

32
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:15.668
park. "He's with a girl on a bike," said

33
00:02:15.669 --> 00:02:19.572
Josh. In a few minutes, we had reached Mr.

34
00:02:19.573 --> 00:02:22.599
Bright. "Hi, Mr. Bright!" said

35
00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.599
Molly. "We saw you at our school

36
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.874
today." "You were a great audience," said Mr.

37
00:02:29.875 --> 00:02:32.370
Bright. He turned to the girl on the

38
00:02:32.371 --> 00:02:35.155
bike. "This is my daughter, Emily."

39
00:02:35.156 --> 00:02:38.089
"Hi," said Emily.

40
00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.481
"I'm glad to see you kids again," said Mr. Bright.

41
00:02:42.482 --> 00:02:45.963
"There was someone I wanted to talk to at your school today.

42
00:02:45.964 --> 00:02:50.239
He wrote about a really great invention, but I can't remember his name."

43
00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.372
"What was the invention?" asked Josh.

44
00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:59.136
"It was called the Fabulous Glasses-Finder," said Mr. Bright.

45
00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:01.174
I couldn't believe it.

46
00:03:01.175 --> 00:03:05.184
"That was my invention!" I cried.

47
00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:09.348
"It's a very interesting idea," said Mr. Bright.

48
00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:14.202
"The only problem is that your glasses-finder is not easy to use."

49
00:03:14.203 --> 00:03:16.564
My heart sank.

50
00:03:16.565 --> 00:03:24.871
"However," said Mr. Bright, "the invention works well for objects bigger than glasses, like bicycles!"

51
00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:29.564
I smiled. "Really?"

52
00:03:29.565 --> 00:03:35.018
"Yes," said Mr. Bright. "Tell them, Emily."

53
00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:39.039
"I ride my bike to school every day," she said.

54
00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.101
"Most kids at my school do.

55
00:03:41.102 --> 00:03:45.545
Sometimes there are so many bikes in the racks, it's hard to find yours.

56
00:03:45.546 --> 00:03:48.930
So I put a flower on my handlebars.

57
00:03:48.931 --> 00:03:53.720
And now I can spot my bike right away!"

58
00:03:53.721 --> 00:03:57.758
"It's a brilliant idea!" said Mr. Bright.

59
00:03:57.759 --> 00:04:01.545
I smiled, but something was bothering me.

60
00:04:01.546 --> 00:04:06.518
"But I didn't actually invent a bicycle-finder," I said.

61
00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:10.219
"Of course you did," said Mr. Bright.

62
00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:15.548
"Sometimes a person invents something, and someone else finds another use for it.

63
00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:18.696
That's part of solving problems."

64
00:04:18.697 --> 00:04:22.055
I thought about the number machine at the bakery.

65
00:04:22.056 --> 00:04:26.173
That invention had given me the idea for the Pick-a-Number.

66
00:04:26.174 --> 00:04:31.948
"Be sure to write about another invention next time I visit your school," said Mr. Bright.

67
00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:36.252
"Okay," I said. I grinned happily.

68
00:04:36.253 --> 00:04:40.084
I had solved a problem on the playground.

69
00:04:40.085 --> 00:04:43.959
I had figured out why Jenny was having trouble in school.

70
00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.739
I had inspired Evan.

71
00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:52.814
And now, with Mr. Bright's help, I had invented a bicycle-finder.

72
00:04:52.815 --> 00:04:56.327
I, Iggy, hadn't won the contest at school.

73
00:04:56.328 --> 00:05:04.209
But I was still an incredible inventor!

